THOUGHT: The NullAway error is because `XmlUtilities.read` can return a nullable `Tileset`, and we dereference it without a null-check. To fix only this error, I’ll add a null check and throw an appropriate exception if it’s null, without changing other behavior. I’ll then run the Gradle compile to ensure the total NullAway error count decreases by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '19,21c\      Tileset tileset = XmlUtilities.read(Tileset.class, resourceName);
      if (tileset == null) {
        throw new TmxException("Failed to load tileset: " + resourceName);
      }
      tileset.finish(resourceName);
      return tileset;' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/resources/Tilesets.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway: .*errors" -n new_build_output.log || sed -n '1,120p' new_build_output.log
```

